          <msContents>
            <summary>[li]Bergamo: Extracts from the 'Liber Privilegiorum': 'Li sopra citati Capitoli sono stampati nel Libretto intitolato 'Ordini circa il Governo del Sacro Monte dell'Abbondanza' nell' Anno 1644' (ff.4-9).[/li][li][Printed]: Bergamo. Ordini circa il governo del Sacro Monte dell' Abbondanza. Bergamo: M. A. Rossi. 1635 (ff.10-23).[/li][li][Anon.]: Collection of 12 Italian poems. The first is entitled 'Capitolo in dishonor della creanza di Giacomo Maria Susio Mirando[lano]', and is followed by Pasquinades in the form of Dialogues between Pasquino and Marforio. There are also the 'Lamenti del Duca di Milano', and a longer work beginning 'Vergine bella nata in mezzo l'acque / Del gran padre Adria figliola et sposa'. This is followed by a second copy of the same by different contemporary hands, and containing a greater number of lines. [c. 1575] (ff. 24-60, of which ff. 46v-55 are blank).[/li][li]Herbal: In Italian, apparently incomplete at each end (ff. 61-98). Illustrated with 75 crude water-colour drawings of medicinal plants in the style of the earliest printed herbals; in many cases the artist has added human or animal details to the pictures. On fol. 75 is a depiction of a female mandrake. [/li][li]Pasted inside the upper cover is a slip headed `Miscellanea' with a short list of contents in Italian, by an anonymous 18th century owner and a shelf mark.[/li]</summary>
            <textLang mainLang="" source="IANA">Latin</textLang>
